		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Re: Any smart ideas on contact resolution priorities?]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=34069#p34069"><![CDATA[
Randy is right. You should sort your contacts such that static contacts are always solved last. This way you reduce chances that stuff gets pushed out of the world.<br><br>For doors I would use motors instead of kinematic bodies. You compute a motor force that will follow the animation. A kinematic body has essentially an infinite force which you want to avoid. This is helpful for all kind of stuff like e.g. also elevators. The down side is that you can now block doors and elevators with e.g. crates that get pushed around. Other solutions as e.g. shadow controllers are very complicated and I would try to avoid those.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=14">Dirk Gregorius</a> — Sun Sep 28, 2014 4:17 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
