		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Any smart ideas on contact resolution priorities?]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=34063#p34063"><![CDATA[
Hi there. Currently in our engine we have three classes of bodies: static bodies, dynamic bodies, and keyframed bodies. One of my team members came to me and asked if there was any way to prioritize responses to collisions between these bodies. For example, if a keyframed gate animates onto a dynamic player, he will push through the static floor, but perhaps the floor should never be allowed to be penetrated, or at least not penetrated 'as much'.<br><br>To me this sounds odd - if the objects are penetrating, between a rock and a hard place, the dynamic player has no where to go. I also can't think how I would factor this kind of thing into the relatively simple gauss seidel solver we use. However, I thought I would ask if anyone has any smart ideas (beyond disabling the contact once collision occurs).<br><br>S<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=10211">sphet</a> — Fri Sep 26, 2014 7:16 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
